CM_ SG_ 288 Odometer "TIER A confirmed: 32-bit accumulator at 1/64 km. Whole drive 196258->196813 = 555 counts = 8.672 km; dash floor()'d 3066.531 -> 3075.203 as 3066 -> 3075. Mid-drive file shows 29 monotonic +1 steps, proving the low 6 bits are a fraction.";
CM_ BO_ 288 "100 ms, DLC 5. Byte 4 unused (always 0x00). TIER A confirmed";
CM_ SG_ 874 StateOfCharge "TIER A confirmed: four dash matches - 89, 86, 83, 84 % (raw 178/172/166/168).";
CM_ SG_ 874 VehicleSpeed "TIER A confirmed: reads exactly 0 when parked and at the end of the last moving file (dash photo: 0 km/h). Integrated over 4.13 km of driving it lands 2.5% under the odometer - see SPEED SCALE note in docs/MG_WINDSOR_DECODE.md. Uses the same 1/64 quantum as the odometer. Max observed 56.0 km/h.";
CM_ SG_ 874 Checksum "sum(bytes0..6)&0xFF, verified 205/205";
CM_ BO_ 874 "100 ms. Carries SoC AND vehicle speed. TIER A confirmed";
CM_ SG_ 364 VehicleSpeedSigned "TIER A confirmed: sits at exactly 0x8000 when stationary, so it is offset-signed (negative = reverse). Agrees with 0x36A VehicleSpeed to ~1% sample by sample. 10 ms rate makes this the better source for dynamics.";
CM_ BO_ 364 "10 ms. Signed high-resolution speed.";
CM_ SG_ 1221 RangeToEmpty "TIER A confirmed: three dash matches - 284, 274, 263 km. The 12-bit x0.5 alternative yields 1161 and is excluded.";
CM_ BO_ 1221 "100 ms. TIER A confirmed";
CM_ SG_ 666 PackVoltage "Cross-validated: sum of 114 cells == reported pack voltage to 0.011%";
CM_ SG_ 666 HvUnknown_B23 "Static 421.8; possibly a voltage limit. UNCONFIRMED.";
CM_ SG_ 666 PackVoltage2 "Second pack-voltage witness";
CM_ BO_ 666 "50 ms. No checksum on this frame (bytes 6-7 always 0x0000).";
CM_ SG_ 647 PackCurrent "TIER A confirmed: (raw-10000)x0.1. SIGN CONFIRMED - charging log reads -7.0 A (x380.7 V = 2.7 kW slow AC charge, SOC rose 83->84). Positive = discharge. Drive range -23.2 A regen .. +67.1 A.";
CM_ SG_ 647 PackVoltage "Cross-validated: sum of 114 cells == reported pack voltage to 0.011%";
CM_ SG_ 647 AuxCurrent "TIER C. Previously mislabelled a second pack current - it is NOT: it stayed 0..4.9 A while PackCurrent swung -23..+67 A during the drive. Identity unknown (possibly an auxiliary/DC-DC load).";
CM_ SG_ 647 Checksum "sum(bytes0..6)&0xFF, verified 410/410";
CM_ BO_ 647 "50 ms, most dynamic HV frame.";
CM_ SG_ 644 PackVoltage "Cross-validated: sum of 114 cells == reported pack voltage to 0.011%";
CM_ BO_ 644 "100 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 667 CellVoltMax "Matches the 0x5A1-0x5C0 block maximum";
CM_ SG_ 667 CellVoltMaxIndex "Observed 1..113 - fits a 114-cell pack";
CM_ SG_ 667 CellVoltMin "Matches the block minimum exactly";
CM_ SG_ 667 CellVoltAvg "TIER B: reads the block min rather than its mean in some samples.";
CM_ BO_ 667 "100 ms BMS summary. Cross-validated: sum of 114 cells == reported pack voltage to 0.011%";
CM_ SG_ 686 Temp1 "TIER B: 47 C; -40 offset assumed";
CM_ SG_ 686 Temp2 "TIER B: 46 C";
CM_ SG_ 686 Temp3 "TIER B: 46 C";
CM_ SG_ 686 Checksum "sum(bytes0..6)&0xFF, verified 205/205";
CM_ BO_ 686 "100 ms. Sensor identity (module/coolant/ambient) unconfirmed.";
CM_ SG_ 1465 SohPercent "TIER B: reads 88; SOH interpretation unproven";
CM_ SG_ 1465 SocPercent "TIER B: reads 89, agrees with 0x36A at 1 % resolution";
CM_ BO_ 1465 "1 Hz. Inside the cell-block ID range but carries no cell words.";
CM_ SG_ 878 TimeToFullCharge "TIER A: reads 0 in every non-charging capture. Across the five charging captures (one continuous device clock, 118.7-480.8 s) it counts down at -1.01 per minute - so the unit is MINUTES. Read 182 min at 83% SoC on a 2.66 kW AC charge; a naive (17% x 38 kWh)/2.66 kW = 152 min, the BMS being conservative about LFP taper. Modelled 16-bit because byte1 (always 0 here) must carry the high byte for any charge longer than 255 min - UNVERIFIED. A transient 0xFF at buffer start looks like a not-available marker.";
CM_ BO_ 878 "100 ms. Static (all zero) whenever the car is not charging.";
CM_ SG_ 661 ChargingActive "TIER A: discriminates cleanly across all three regimes (parked+AC-on / driving / charging) over 11 captures. 1 = charging.";
CM_ SG_ 661 ChargerCableStatus "TIER A field / TIER B name. Cross-confirmed by the MG Comet EV pack (oem_packs/MG/Comet/EV_2024) — an independent RE of a different MG EV on the same platform, which calls this bit range Charger_Cable_Status at the identical 10|2 position. Reads 0 across 1230 frames of parked/driving and 1 across 769 frames of charging. The 'cable' reading is the Comet author's, not ours: with no plugged-in-but-idle capture we still cannot separate CONNECTED from CHARGING.";
CM_ BO_ 661 "100 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 1158 CellTemp_B6 "TIER B. Cross-confirmed by the MG Comet EV pack (oem_packs/MG/Comet/EV_2024) — an independent RE of a different MG EV on the same platform (Max_cell_Temp at 55|8, offset -40). Windsor readings cool coherently over the session: 53 C parked in the sun -> 49 mid-drive -> 47 after moving and while charging. NOTE the Comet labels byte6 max and byte7 min, but on the Windsor byte6 <= byte7 in every sample, so that max/min assignment does NOT hold here and is deliberately not claimed.";
CM_ SG_ 1158 CellTemp_B7 "TIER B. See CellTemp_B6.";
CM_ BO_ 1158 "100 ms. Frame found only because the Comet pack pointed at it.";
CM_ SG_ 840 VehicleSpeed3 "TIER A: a third speed witness, found via Cross-confirmed by the MG Comet EV pack (oem_packs/MG/Comet/EV_2024) — an independent RE of a different MG EV on the same platform. Scale derived by ratio against our proven 0x36A speed over two files with very different averages (36.5 and 6.9 km/h): implied 0.019938 and 0.019995 — agreeing to 0.3%, so 0.02 km/h (1/50). Reads exactly 0 when parked. The Comet DBC's own 0.0311 does not fit the Windsor.";
CM_ BO_ 840 "10 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 357 PropulsionMode "TIER A: discriminates cleanly across all three regimes (parked+AC-on / driving / charging) over 11 captures. 1 = parked/driving, 0 = charging.";
CM_ SG_ 357 PropulsionMode2 "TIER A: discriminates cleanly across all three regimes (parked+AC-on / driving / charging) over 11 captures. Tracks PropulsionMode.";
CM_ SG_ 357 ChargeMode "TIER A: discriminates cleanly across all three regimes (parked+AC-on / driving / charging) over 11 captures. 1 = charging (inverse of PropulsionMode).";
CM_ BO_ 357 "10 ms. HV system mode - propulsion vs charging.";
CM_ SG_ 1270 ChargerState "TIER B: 0x14 not charging -> 0x08 charging. A charger-type/state enum plausibly lives here, but ONE charger type was captured so no mapping is claimed.";
CM_ SG_ 1270 ChargerParam_B2 "TIER C: 0 unless charging, then 75. Does not reconcile with 2.66 kW at 230 V as either amps or amps/10. Unidentified.";
CM_ SG_ 1270 AcMainsVoltage "TIER B: 0 unless charging, then 230 - exactly Indian mains nominal. Scale 1 V assumed; only one supply voltage was ever seen.";
CM_ BO_ 1270 "100 ms. Only this frame changes shape wholesale when the cable is live, so it is almost certainly the on-board charger.";
CM_ SG_ 341 AccelPedalPos "TIER A confirmed: sweeps the full 0..100 range in the Pedal Position log.";
CM_ SG_ 341 GearSelector "TIER A confirmed: 3=P is constant across EVERY stationary capture; 1=D is constant across every forward-driving file; 2=R occurs in exactly the two files where the 0x16C signed speed goes negative (-4.05 km/h, reversing out of a parking spot) - the two signals confirm each other. 0=N by elimination. Matches the After-Moving dash photo (D).";
CM_ SG_ 341 AccelPedalPos2 "TIER A confirmed: byte-for-byte identical to AccelPedalPos - redundant sensor channel.";
CM_ SG_ 341 PropulsionEnabled "TIER A: discriminates cleanly across all three regimes (parked+AC-on / driving / charging) over 11 captures. 1 = parked/driving, 0 = charging.";
CM_ BO_ 341 "10 ms. Mirrored on MS CAN with identical content.";
CM_ SG_ 298 DoorState_1 "TIER C: a door, position not established (never actuated).";
CM_ SG_ 298 DoorPassenger "TIER A confirmed: 0xAA<->0xBA over two open/close cycles.";
CM_ SG_ 298 DoorState_3 "TIER C: a door, position not established (never actuated).";
CM_ SG_ 298 DoorDriver "TIER A confirmed: 0xAA<->0xAB over three open/close cycles.";
CM_ BO_ 298 "100 ms. Byte 2 = four 2-bit door fields (0xAA = all closed & unlocked). All four read 0 when the car is locked. Driver and passenger verified by event-isolated captures; the other two are unactuated.";
CM_ SG_ 225 DriverSeatBelt "TIER A confirmed: byte1 0x00<->0x08 across two buckle cycles. POLARITY RESOLVED — reads 1 through the whole last moving file, and the dash photo taken at that moment shows 'Fasten the seatbelt'. So 1 = UNBUCKLED.";
CM_ SG_ 225 Checksum "sum(bytes0..6)&0xFF, verified 41/41";
CM_ BO_ 225 "500 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 663 HazardSwitch "TIER B: byte4 0x40 -> 0x00, one clean transition (switch state, not lamp - it does not blink).";
CM_ SG_ 663 TurnUnknown_bit32 "TIER C: byte4 0x80, seen during the Gear log.";
CM_ BO_ 663 "50 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 633 LightSwitchState "TIER B: stepped 2->3->4->5 while the switch was rotated (baseline 2). Position labels NOT established - needs a per-position capture.";
CM_ BO_ 633 "20 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 1083 AcState "TIER B: 1<->2 across the AC toggle. Mirrored on MS CAN.";
CM_ BO_ 1083 "100 ms, present on both HS and MS CAN.";
CM_ SG_ 1008 HvacActive1 "TIER A confirmed: 0 while AC off, ramps 9..22 when on; non-zero in the AC-ON baseline.";
CM_ SG_ 1008 HvacTemp "TIER C: 62..65, possibly a temperature.";
CM_ SG_ 1008 HvacActive2 "TIER A confirmed: tracks HvacActive1.";
CM_ SG_ 1008 HvacActive3 "TIER A confirmed: 0 when off, ramps to 30.";
CM_ BO_ 1008 "MS CAN, 100 ms. The climate frame.";
CM_ SG_ 651 BrakeSignal "TIER B: 0x7C<->0x86 on the brake press (baseline 0x22). Two-state, not a pressure ramp, so the physical meaning is unproven.";
CM_ SG_ 651 BrakeSignal2 "Mirror of BrakeSignal (0x28B duplicates bytes 0-3 into 4-7).";
CM_ BO_ 651 "50 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 1381 ParkBrakeCandidate "TIER C - NOT CONFIRMED. Toggles in the Parking Brake log but ALSO in the Pedal and RPM logs, so it is more likely 'brake applied' or 'stationary' than EPB.";
CM_ BO_ 1381 "100 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 1471 CellVolt_115 "Slot not populated (reads 0xFFF)";
CM_ SG_ 1471 CellVolt_116 "Slot not populated (reads 0xFFF)";
CM_ SG_ 1472 CellVolt_117 "Slot not populated (reads 0xFFF)";
CM_ SG_ 1472 CellVolt_118 "Slot not populated (reads 0xFFF)";
CM_ SG_ 1472 CellVolt_119 "Slot not populated (reads 0xFFF)";
CM_ SG_ 1472 CellVolt_120 "Slot not populated (reads 0xFFF)";
CM_ BO_ 1441 "Cell block 0x5A1-0x5C0 @ 1 Hz. Each 16-bit word = [3-bit slot 1..4][1-bit not-present][12-bit cell mV]; structure verified on 2400/2400 words. On the PRO 98 cells are populated -> 98S (the standard Windsor is 114S). Slots beyond that read 0xFFF. Cell NUMBERING is assumed sequential by ID then word; physical mapping unconfirmed.";
VAL_ 661 ChargerCableStatus 0 "Disconnected" 1 "Connected" ;
VAL_ 341 GearSelector 0 "N" 1 "D" 2 "R" 3 "P" ;
VAL_ 298 DoorState_1 0 "Locked/NotAvailable" 2 "Closed" 3 "Open" ;
VAL_ 298 DoorPassenger 0 "Locked/NotAvailable" 2 "Closed" 3 "Open" ;
VAL_ 298 DoorState_3 0 "Locked/NotAvailable" 2 "Closed" 3 "Open" ;
VAL_ 298 DoorDriver 0 "Locked/NotAvailable" 2 "Closed" 3 "Open" ;
VAL_ 225 DriverSeatBelt 0 "Buckled" 1 "Unbuckled" ;
